-- title:
--   Reducedness of the localised weight-2 Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N$ and a set $S$ of natural numbers such that every prime $q$ dividing $N$ belongs to $S$. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero that is complete with respect to its maximal ideal, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-$2$ Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$; here [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the space of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ attached to primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ attached to primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$ (under the hypothesis on $S$ no generator of the second kind occurs). The conclusion is that the ring [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131), defined as the localisation of `heckeBaseAlgebra N S 𝒪` at the submonoid obtained by pushing the prime complement of the ideal `heckeCharKernel N S 𝒪 θ` forward along `latticeBaseChange N S 𝒪`, is reduced: it has no nonzero nilpotent elements. Nothing further is asserted — in particular not that this ring is a domain, nor anything about its rank or its residue field.
--
--   This is the localised form, at a residual Hecke eigensystem $\theta$ with coefficients in the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, of the reducedness of the weight-$2$ Hecke algebra of level $N$ away from $S$, and it is deduced from [`CuspForm.isReduced_heckeAlgebra_of_primeFactors_subset`](thm.html#CuspForm.isReduced_heckeAlgebra_of_primeFactors_subset). It is the input used throughout the project wherever the local Hecke ring attached to $\theta$ must be known to have no nilpotents, for instance in the construction of the associated Galois representation data and in the flatness and ordinarity statements built on them.
-- source:
